es_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproduced in Godot 4.5, 4.4 .... And master\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nCurrently, when window calculate its minsize:\n```\nSize2 Window::get_contents_minimum_size() const {\n\tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2());\n\tVector2 ms;\n\tif (GDVIRTUAL_CALL(_get_contents_minimum_size, ms)) {\n\t\treturn ms;\n\t}\n\treturn _get_contents_minimum_size();\n}\n\nSize2 Window::get_clamped_minimum_size() const {\n\tERR_READ_THREAD_GUARD_V(Size2());\n\tif (!wrap_controls) {\n\t\treturn min_size;\n\t}\n\n\treturn min_size.max(get_contents_minimum_size() * get_content_scale_factor());\n}\n```\nget_clamped_minimum_size() do assume get_contents_minimum_size() return size without content_scale_factor, however: \n```\nSize2 Window::_get_contents_minimum_size() const {\n\tSize2 max;\n\n\tfor (int i = 0; i < get_child_count(); i++) {\n\t\tControl *c = Object::cast_to<Control>(get_child(i));\n\t\tif (c) {\n\t\t\tPoint2i pos = c->get_position();\n\t\t\tSize2i min = c->get_combined_minimum_size();\n\n\t\t\tmax = max.max(pos + min);\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\n\treturn max * content_scale_factor;\n}\n```\nWindow::_get_contents_minimum_size(）applied content_scale_factor itself.\nThe inheritance of Window, like Popup/PopupMenu, _get_contents_minimum_size() returns size without content_scale_factor, which is supposed  to be correct.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNo need\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNo need","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aki